> So hey, while we're talking about keystrokes, how exactly does one
> undertake twoweaponing?

#twoweapon

The game will automatically expand the rest of
the word as soon and it is unambiguous just like
all of the other dash-commands, so do it one
letter at a time at first.  You'll quickly get
used to letting it finish for you.  Some
hash-commands take one letter, some two.

It will tell you that you begin two weapon combat
or it will tell you that you resume using your
primary weapon (or it will tell you you can't do
it).

You need to have a primary and secondary weapon
first.  Use w to wield, x to switch (to maybe
nothing), w to wield, i to figure out if you
currently have primary and secondary the way
you want.



